{"agent":"pperf8","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The confirmed inline-bound defect is not fixed; the write path now drops file content entirely. Intent and PM-remote require the remote/shell-less answer to include the exact command and the SVG/HTML inline up to a bound, because the server may not share a filesystem with the user. Given `format=\"svg\"` (or `html`), `run_perf_report` still writes `doc` to `path` but sets `body` to only `path: {path}` plus `_footer`, so `Outcome.text` never contains any of the document and there is still no bound. A host with no shared filesystem cannot open that path, and the chat answer is not the report.","digest":"26e913060733d241","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/perfreport.py:176","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/perfreport.py:176"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_next_calls` still interpolates `out` unquoted. Given `out=\"my report.html\"` and `win=\"7d\"`, the CLI string is `ddflow perf report --format html --window 7d --out my report.html` (MCP: `out=my report.html`). Copying that “exact” next call splits on the space, so `--out` does not receive the path that was just written.","digest":"a419a37cd4eaf3a6","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/perfreport.py:84","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/perfreport.py:84"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":2,"delta_from":"4960a481f01c586e289819aedd29d28209600082","delta_raised":["26e913060733d241","a419a37cd4eaf3a6"],"delta_rounds":2,"diff_chars":4228,"diff_sha":"7281256f28f2b04875b561bf9298f4f372ccb4c9c5de8c61dfc75defae4f5c15","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 4960a481f0","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":33.8,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"1153c78d73e6a9e8","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PM-report-surfaces.rub